# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  x25519.la — X25519_KIT: RFC 7748 X25519 Diffie-Hellman (NET_DESIGN.md 1).
#
#  WHAT. The one public-key primitive LogosNet needs: Curve25519's
#  x-coordinate scalar multiplication, the function X25519 of RFC 7748
#  section 5, and its two uses in section 6.1.
#
#      X25519_KIT(str_at)(ord)(str_to_int)(int_to_str)(chr)(concat)(str_len)
#                (error)(add)(sub)(mul)(lt)(int_eq)(band)(bor)(bxor)(bshl)(bshr)
#        -> la s. s(scalarmult)(public)(shared)
#
#    scalarmult(k)(u)  k and u are 32-byte strings; the result is the 32-byte
#                      u-coordinate of k * u. k is clamped (k[0] &= 248,
#                      k[31] &= 127, k[31] |= 64); u is read little-endian
#                      with its top bit masked, and a non-canonical u >= p is
#                      accepted as the RFC requires; the result is fully
#                      reduced mod p = 2^255 - 19. Any other length halts:
#                      "x25519: scalarmult: key and point must be 32 bytes".
#    public(sk)        scalarmult(sk)(9): the public key of sk. A key that
#                      is not 32 bytes halts: "x25519: public: key must be
#                      32 bytes".
#    shared(sk)(pk)    an option, la none. la some. ...: none(none) when the
#                      result is all zero (pk of small order, RFC 7748 6.1),
#                      some(secret) otherwise. A key or point that is not 32
#                      bytes halts: "x25519: shared: key and point must be 32
#                      bytes".
#  Each halt names its own operation, as NET_DESIGN.md's shared rule asks
#  (<module>: <operation>: <reason>).
#
#  The constructor takes the same builtins as logoscrypt.la's CRYPT_FAST, in
#  the same order.
#
#  HOW IT IS USED. Build the record ONCE at startup and pass it on as a value:
#      import("x25519.la")
#      ... X25519_KIT(str_at)(ord)(str_to_int)(int_to_str)(chr)(concat)
#                    (str_len)(error)(add)(sub)(mul)(lt)(int_eq)(band)(bor)
#                    (bxor)(bshl)(bshr)
#            (la scalarmult. la public. la shared. ...)
#
#  THE FIELD. An element of GF(p) is a record of ten limbs la k. k(f0)..(f9)
#  in radix 2^25.5, as in ref10: limb i is weighted 2^w(i), w(i) = ceil(25.5 i)
#  = 0 26 51 77 102 128 153 179 204 230, and is 26 bits wide for even i, 25
#  for odd. Limbs are NON-NEGATIVE native integers: the VM's bshr is a
#  logical shift, so a carry is a plain shift and mask, and a difference
#  x - y is computed as x + 2p - y.
#
#  WHY EVERY INTERMEDIATE FITS A SIGNED 64-BIT INTEGER (gate_x25519.sh
#  recomputes these numbers, and runs the kernels on operands at the limits).
#   - "Carried" is what the carry chain returns: limbs below 2^26 (even) and
#     2^25 (odd), except that limb 1 may exceed 2^25 - 1 by at most 1711.
#   - The ladder multiplies only three classes of operand: carried; a sum of
#     two carried elements (limbs below twice the carried bound); and a
#     difference x + 2p - y of two carried elements (limbs below the carried
#     bound plus 2p's limb, about 3 x 2^26 and 3 x 2^25). A difference never
#     goes negative: every carried limb is at most 2p's (2^27-38, then
#     2^26-2 for odd limbs, 2^27-2 for even).
#   - Column k of a product is the sum of f_i g_j over i+j = k plus 19 times
#     the sum over i+j = k+10, each term doubled when i and j are both odd
#     (2^w(i) 2^w(j) = 2 * 2^w(i+j) then; 2^255 = 19 mod p). Its largest
#     value, for two differences, is 5.046e18 = 2^62.13 < 2^63 = 9.223e18;
#     difference x sum gives 2^61.55, sum x sum 2^60.96, carried x carried
#     2^58.96. A kernel adds non-negative terms, so every partial sum and
#     every scaled group is below its column.
#   - The carry chain (t1 = h1 + h0>>26, t2 = h2 + t1>>25, ..., t9 = h9 +
#     t8>>26, u0 = (h0 & M26) + 19 (t9>>25), limb 1 = (t1 & M25) + u0>>26)
#     stays below 2^62.13 + 2^37; with the column bounds above, u0>>26 is at
#     most 1711, which is where the carried bound of limb 1 comes from.
#   - T = AA + 121665 E (E a difference) has limbs below 2^44.5, and is
#     carried before it is multiplied.
#   - A carried element is below 2^255 + 2^37 < 2p, so the final reduction
#     is one conditional subtraction of p, done without a branch: q = 1 iff
#     v >= p is the carry out of v + 19, then v + 19q with bit 255 dropped.
#
#  THE LADDER (RFC 7748 section 5). 255 steps, bit 254 down to bit 0, with
#  the same operations for every bit: nothing branches on a key bit. The RFC
#  swaps (x2,z2) and (x3,z3) when the bit changes, then doubles slot 2 and
#  adds the two slots. Here the swap is an arithmetic SELECT of the slot to
#  double, (f & ~m) | (g & m) limb by limb, with m = 0 or -1 from
#  c = k[t+1] xor k[t] (k[255] = 0), exactly the RFC's swap bit. The
#  differential addition (x3 = (DA+CB)^2, z3 = x1 (DA-CB)^2) needs no swap:
#  exchanging the two slots exchanges DA and CB, which only changes the sign
#  of DA-CB, and that is squared. After bit 0 the result's slot is selected
#  with k[0] (the RFC's final cswap), and x2 * z2^(p-2) (ref10's chain:
#  254 squarings and 11 multiplications) is fully reduced and encoded.
#  a24 = 121665, in z2 = E (AA + a24 E).
#
#  WHY IT IS FAST. On the SECD VM (WM_DESIGN.md "How fast the VM is",
#  confirmed here): every name bound over a body costs one more scan of that
#  body (CLOSE scans what it closes, about a nanosecond a byte); looking a
#  name up walks the environment cell by cell (about 3.5 ns a cell); naming
#  a glyph or a builtin walks the program. So:
#   - the field operations are straight-line kernels (the generated section
#     below), glyphs whose parameters are the builtins and constants they
#     use, applied once when the kit is built, with one-letter names so the
#     scanned text is short;
#   - in the 10x10 multiplication the first operand's limbs arrive as the
#     partial applications mul(f_i) (X25519_TOPA), so each of its 100
#     products is a single application f_i(g_j), and add, used 90 times, is
#     its LAST parameter, the first name a lookup finds (likewise mul and
#     add in the squaring, and the select masks in the select);
#   - sums, differences and selects are lazy records: their limbs are
#     computed when the next kernel reads them;
#   - constants are parameters; booleans are applied to thunks.
#
#  THE GENERATED SECTION. X25519_MULC, X25519_SQC, X25519_CARRY, X25519_TOPA,
#  X25519_L2, X25519_SQSEL, X25519_SEL and X25519_ETK are written by
#  x25519_gen.la, a Lingua Adamica program committed beside this file;
#  gate_x25519.sh regenerates them and requires the same bytes.
#
#  MEASURED on the VM, CPU time inside the program (gate_x25519.sh), on a
#  4-core machine at load average 8 to 16: one scalarmult, public or shared
#  about 0.10 s of CPU (0.26 to 0.30 s of wall time at that load); one ladder
#  step about 0.4 ms; within it a multiplication about 37 us and a squaring
#  about 23 us, each including its 8 us carry. Building the kit takes about
#  1 ms. The C host needs about two minutes for one scalarmult.
#
#  ENGINES. Pure Lingua Adamica over the int and bitwise builtins, so the C
#  host gives the same bytes (the gate runs one scalarmult there), some
#  hundreds of times more slowly; the VM is the engine.
#
#  HONESTLY OUT OF SCOPE
#   - Constant time. No branch depends on a secret bit and the zero test in
#     shared has no early exit, but the VM interprets and allocates: no
#     timing claim is made about this engine.
#   - Validation beyond RFC 7748 6.1's all-zero check (X25519 needs none).
#   - Signatures (Ed25519): NET_DESIGN.md, "Out of scope now".
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

export X25519_KIT

glyph Z = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))
glyph LET = la v. la k. k(v)

# ── the field kernels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MULC(u t w K)(a..j)(A..J)(p): the product's ten columns to K (the carry);
#   a..j are mul(f_i), A..J the second operand's limbs, u t w = x2 x19 x38.
# SQC(u q t w o K)(a..j)(m)(p): the square's columns to K; u q t w o = x2 x4
#   x19 x38 x76.
# CARRY(p r n m t S s)(h0..h9): the carried record (r = bshr, n m the 26- and
#   25-bit masks, t = x19, S s = 26 25).
# TOPA(m)(X)(K): K applied to mul(x_i) for X's limbs.
# L2(p s Q O R)(a..j)(A..J)(K): K(a+A)(a-A+2p), both lazy records.
# SQSEL(z m p)(a..j)(A..J)(o n y): the square of the select, through z.
# SEL(a..j)(A..J)(o n y): the select as a lazy record; o = bor.
# ETK(p s v m Q O R K z)(a..j)(A..J): z(E)(K(T)), E = a - A + 2p as mul
#   partials, T = a + 121665 E (v = x121665) through the carry K.
# >>> generated by x25519_gen.la (do not edit by hand)
glyph X25519_MULC = la u. la t. la w. la K.
    la a. la b. la c. la d. la e. la f. la g. la h. la i. la j.
    la A. la B. la C. la D. la E. la F. la G. la H. la I. la J. la p. K
  (p(p(a(A))(t(p(p(p(c(I))(e(G)))(g(E)))(i(C)))))(w(p(p(p(p(b(J))(d(H)))(f(F)))(h(D)))(j(B)))))
  (p(p(a(B))(b(A)))(t(p(p(p(p(p(p(p(c(J))(d(I)))(e(H)))(f(G)))(g(F)))(h(E)))(i(D)))(j(C)))))
  (p(p(p(p(a(C))(c(A)))(u(b(B))))(t(p(p(e(I))(g(G)))(i(E)))))(w(p(p(p(d(J))(f(H)))(h(F)))(j(D)))))
  (p(p(p(p(a(D))(b(C)))(c(B)))(d(A)))(t(p(p(p(p(p(e(J))(f(I)))(g(H)))(h(G)))(i(F)))(j(E)))))
  (p(p(p(p(p(a(E))(c(C)))(e(A)))(u(p(b(D))(d(B)))))(t(p(g(I))(i(G)))))(w(p(p(f(J))(h(H)))(j(F)))))
  (p(p(p(p(p(p(a(F))(b(E)))(c(D)))(d(C)))(e(B)))(f(A)))(t(p(p(p(g(J))(h(I)))(i(H)))(j(G)))))
  (p(p(p(p(p(p(a(G))(c(E)))(e(C)))(g(A)))(u(p(p(b(F))(d(D)))(f(B)))))(t(i(I))))(w(p(h(J))(j(H)))))
  (p(p(p(p(p(p(p(p(a(H))(b(G)))(c(F)))(d(E)))(e(D)))(f(C)))(g(B)))(h(A)))(t(p(i(J))(j(I)))))
  (p(p(p(p(p(p(a(I))(c(G)))(e(E)))(g(C)))(i(A)))(u(p(p(p(b(H))(d(F)))(f(D)))(h(B)))))(w(j(J))))
  (p(p(p(p(p(p(p(p(p(a(J))(b(I)))(c(H)))(d(G)))(e(F)))(f(E)))(g(D)))(h(C)))(i(B)))(j(A)))
glyph X25519_SQC = la u. la q. la t. la w. la o. la K.
    la a. la b. la c. la d. la e. la f. la g. la h. la i. la j. la m. la p. K
  (p(p(m(a)(a))(w(p(p(m(c)(i))(m(e)(g)))(m(f)(f)))))(o(p(m(b)(j))(m(d)(h)))))
  (p(u(m(a)(b)))(w(p(p(p(m(c)(j))(m(d)(i)))(m(e)(h)))(m(f)(g)))))
  (p(p(p(u(p(m(a)(c))(m(b)(b))))(t(m(g)(g))))(w(m(e)(i))))(o(p(m(d)(j))(m(f)(h)))))
  (p(u(p(m(a)(d))(m(b)(c))))(w(p(p(m(e)(j))(m(f)(i)))(m(g)(h)))))
  (p(p(p(p(m(c)(c))(u(m(a)(e))))(q(m(b)(d))))(w(p(m(g)(i))(m(h)(h)))))(o(m(f)(j))))
  (p(u(p(p(m(a)(f))(m(b)(e)))(m(c)(d))))(w(p(m(g)(j))(m(h)(i)))))
  (p(p(p(u(p(p(m(a)(g))(m(c)(e)))(m(d)(d))))(q(m(b)(f))))(t(m(i)(i))))(o(m(h)(j))))
  (p(u(p(p(p(m(a)(h))(m(b)(g)))(m(c)(f)))(m(d)(e))))(w(m(i)(j))))
  (p(p(p(m(e)(e))(u(p(m(a)(i))(m(c)(g)))))(q(p(m(b)(h))(m(d)(f)))))(w(m(j)(j))))
  (u(p(p(p(p(m(a)(j))(m(b)(i)))(m(c)(h)))(m(d)(g)))(m(e)(f))))
glyph X25519_CARRY = la p. la r. la n. la m. la t. la S. la s.
    la a. la b. la c. la d. la e. la f. la g. la h. la i. la j.
  (la B. (la C. (la D. (la E. (la F. (la G. (la H. (la I. (la J. (la A.
    la k. k(n(A))(p(m(B))(r(A)(S)))(n(C))(m(D))(n(E))(m(F))(n(G))(m(H))(n(I))(m(J)))
    (p(n(a))(t(r(J)(s)))))
    (p(j)(r(I)(S))))
    (p(i)(r(H)(s))))
    (p(h)(r(G)(S))))
    (p(g)(r(F)(s))))
    (p(f)(r(E)(S))))
    (p(e)(r(D)(s))))
    (p(d)(r(C)(S))))
    (p(c)(r(B)(s))))
