     (p(f)(v(s(p(f)(O))(F))))(p(g)(v(s(p(g)(R))(G))))(p(h)(v(s(p(h)(O))(H))))(p(i)(v(s(p(i)(R))(I))))(p(j)(v(s(p(j)(O))(J)))))
# <<< end of generated section

# ── the ladder step ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One step of the Montgomery ladder. st = la k. k(X)(Z)(U)(W): slot 2 is
# (X, Z) (the point the previous step doubled), slot 3 is (U, W); ny =
# la k. k(n)(y), n = band(~m) and y = band(m) for this bit's select mask m.
#   A = X+Z, B = X-Z, C = U+W, D = U-W                         (l2, lazy)
#   AA = sel(A,C)^2, BB = sel(B,D)^2: the slot to double         (sqsel)
#   DA = D*A, CB = C*B; P = DA+CB, M = DA-CB                    (mulc, l2)
#   the new slot 2 = (AA*BB, E*(AA + a24 E)), E = AA-BB         (mulc, etk)
#   the new slot 3 = (P^2, x1 M^2)                               (sqc, mulx)
# The differential addition is symmetric in the two slots, so only the
# doubling needs the select. The new state's four fields are computed when
# the next step reads them (each is read once).
glyph X25519_STEP = la l2. la sqsel. la topa. la mulc. la etk. la sqc. la add. la mul. la bor. la mulx. la ny. la st.
  ny(la n. la y. st(la X. la Z. la U. la W.
    Z(X(l2))(la A. la B.
    W(U(l2))(la C. la D.
    (la AA. la BB. la DA. la CB.
       CB(DA(l2))(la P. la M.
         la k. k(BB(topa(AA)(mulc))(add))(BB(AA(etk)))(P(sqc)(mul)(add))(M(sqc)(mul)(add)(mulx)(add))))
    (C(A(sqsel))(bor)(n)(y))(D(B(sqsel))(bor)(n)(y))(A(topa(D)(mulc))(add))(B(topa(C)(mulc))(add))))))

# ── the kit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# X25519_KIT(str_at)(ord)(str_to_int)(int_to_str)(chr)(concat)(str_len)(error)
#           (add)(sub)(mul)(lt)(int_eq)(band)(bor)(bxor)(bshl)(bshr)
#   -> la s. s(scalarmult)(public)(shared)
# Everything below the parameter list runs once, when the record is built:
# the constants, the kernels applied to their builtins, the helpers.
glyph X25519_KIT = la str_at. la ord. la str_to_int. la int_to_str. la chr. la concat. la str_len. la error.
    la add. la sub. la mul. la lt. la int_eq. la band. la bor. la bxor. la bshl. la bshr.
 (la C0. la C1. la C2. la C3. la C4. la C5. la C6. la C7. la C8. la C9. la C10. la C12. la C16. la C19. la C20.
  la C22. la C24. la C25. la C26. la C28. la C31. la C32. la C38. la C50. la C64. la C76. la C100. la C127.
  la C248. la C255. la M25. la M26. la Q2. la O2. la R2. la A24.
  LET(Z)(la fix.
  # the kernels; Q2 O2 R2 are 2p's limbs (limb 0, odd limbs, even limbs >= 2)
  LET(X25519_CARRY(add)(bshr)(band(M26))(band(M25))(mul(C19))(C26)(C25))(la carry.
  LET(X25519_MULC(mul(C2))(mul(C19))(mul(C38))(carry))(la mulc.
  LET(X25519_SQC(mul(C2))(mul(C4))(mul(C19))(mul(C38))(mul(C76))(carry))(la sqc.
  LET(X25519_TOPA(mul))(la topa.
  LET(X25519_L2(add)(sub)(Q2)(O2)(R2))(la l2.
  LET(X25519_SQSEL(sqc)(mul)(add))(la sqsel.
  LET(X25519_SEL)(la sel.
  LET(X25519_ETK(add)(sub)(mul(A24))(mul)(Q2)(O2)(R2)(carry)(la E. la T. T(E(mulc))(add)))(la etk.
  LET(X25519_STEP(l2)(sqsel)(topa)(mulc)(etk)(sqc)(add)(mul)(bor))(la step.
  # field multiplication and squaring of records, both carried
  LET(la F. la G. G(topa(F)(mulc))(add))(la fmul.
  LET(la F. F(sqc)(mul)(add))(la sq.
  LET(la n. la F. fix(la go. la n. la F. int_eq(n)(C0)(la _. F)(la _. go(sub(n)(C1))(sq(F)))(C0))(n)(F))(la sqn.
  # z^(p-2) = z^(2^255 - 21): ref10's chain, 254 squarings and 11 multiplications
  LET(la z. (la z2. (la z9. (la z11. (la a5. (la a10. (la a20. (la a40. (la a50. (la a100. (la a200. (la a250.
                 fmul(sqn(C5)(a250))(z11))
               (fmul(sqn(C50)(a200))(a50)))
               (fmul(sqn(C100)(a100))(a100)))
               (fmul(sqn(C50)(a50))(a50)))
               (fmul(sqn(C10)(a40))(a10)))
               (fmul(sqn(C20)(a20))(a20)))
               (fmul(sqn(C10)(a10))(a10)))
               (fmul(sqn(C5)(a5))(a5)))
               (fmul(sq(z11))(z9)))
               (fmul(z9)(z2)))
               (fmul(z)(sq(sq(z2)))))
             (sq(z)))(la inv.
  LET(la n. chr(int_to_str(n)))(la T.
  LET(la s. str_to_int(str_len(s)))(la len.
  # u (32 bytes) -> limbs: limb k is bits w(k)..w(k+1)-1 of the little-endian
  # number, read from the 32-bit word at byte w(k)/8 (w(k) mod 8 plus the
